    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\nWith the latest main branch, mini.ai not able to identify embedded functions, for example bash in markdown.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ad2220d7-4711-4f0e-83a2-e4f912a9ca50)\n\n<pre>\n## Checking test\n\n```bash\necho this is a test file\n\nfunction main() {\n  echo hello there\n}\n```\n</pre>\n\nwith commit \n```lua\nreturn {\n  { commit = \"7c36f6d459bd8a15c77fbfa75fbc843b2c18af87\", \"echasnovski/mini.ai\" },\n}\n```\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a21e71e2-beb5-4360-ab3b-1d82ab4a9d72)\n\n### Reproduction\n\nUse the main branch to produce the issue. \ncommit `7c36f6d459bd8a15c77fbfa75fbc843b2c18af87` doesn't have this issue.",
