            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nThe default `af` textobject is \"function call\" and works in the reproduction steps (as it doesn't require tree-sitter).\n\nAssuming you mean `gen_spec.treesitter()` for function definition (used, for example, in LazyVim), I indeed can reproduce all: not working on latest 'mini.nvim' `main`, working on 5def9231ef1f (and prior), and working with 'nvim-treesitter' on `master` branch (I did not realize that 'nvim-treesitter' computed matches respecting tree-sitter injections).\n\nI'll take a look. In the meantime reverting to working commit (like `stable` branch or `v0.16.0` tag) or setting [`use_nvim_treesitter = true` in `gen_spec.treesitter`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/de0a88d925c8e69fdbb498141207ee43504e5cd1/doc/mini-ai.txt#L769) should fix this.",
